    {
      "ref": "PYQ-PHY-73e75c383c9a",
      "subtopic": "general",
      "type": "single_correct",
      "difficulty": 5,
      "expected_time_sec": 120,
      "source_type": "pyq",
      "exam": "jee_main",
      "year": 2026,
      "shift": "6 Apr 2026, Shift 1",
      "status": "draft",
      "stem": "A LCR series circuit driven with $E_{\\text{rms}} = 90\\,\\text{V}$ at frequency $f_d = 30\\,\\text{Hz}$ has resistance $R = 80\\,\\Omega$ , an inductance with inductive reactance $X_L = 20.0\\,\\Omega$ and capacitance with capacitive reactance $X_C = 80.0\\,\\Omega$. The power factor of the circuit is ______.",
      "image": null,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "content": "0.8",
          "is_correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "content": "0.64",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "content": "0.9",
          "is_correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "content": "0.5",
          "is_correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "In a series LCR circuit the power factor is $\\cos\\phi = \\dfrac{R}{Z}$, where $Z = \\sqrt{R^2 + (X_C - X_L)^2}$.\nThe net reactance is $X_C - X_L = 80.0\\,\\Omega - 20.0\\,\\Omega = 60.0\\,\\Omega$.\nThe impedance is $Z = \\sqrt{(80\\,\\Omega)^2 + (60\\,\\Omega)^2} = \\sqrt{6400 + 3600}\\,\\Omega = 100\\,\\Omega$.\nSo the power factor is $\\cos\\phi = \\dfrac{80\\,\\Omega}{100\\,\\Omega} = 0.8$.\nThe values $E_{\\text{rms}}$ and $f_d$ are not needed to find the power factor.\nAnswer: (A) 0.8"
    }
  ]
